8. VALUE OF INFORMATION TEST
The system must recognize that:
Sometimes the highest-value action is not acting. It is learning enough to act correctly.
If uncertainty materially affects the decision, Naya should evaluate whether obtaining additional information has greater expected value than immediate action.
Conceptually:
VOI = Expected improvement from additional information − Cost of obtaining it
The system should gather information when:
VOI > cost/risk of waiting or investigating
and the information could materially change the decision.

